                                        </div>
                                    
                                    <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                        <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                            <h2 class="type-h3">Louisa Binder</h2>

                                                                                            <p class="type-h5">Hilde Wangel</p>
                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Louisa Binder can currently be seen playing the new love interest in Amazon’s </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your Fault: London, </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">and has recently wrapped filming the final instalment of the trilogy, </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Our Fault: London</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">. She was one of the leads opposite Natasha McElhone in three seasons of </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Hotel Portofino, </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">and recently completed </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Wind of Change</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">; a musical biopic about the legendary German rock band, Scorpions. She’s just finished filming Channel 4’s upcoming series, </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Up To No Good, </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">in which she plays the younger version of Glenn Close’s character.</span></p>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </article>
                            </template>
                                            </li>
                                                                                                                                        
