                        </div>

                                                    <template data-dialog-content="dialog-person-5-8619">
                                <article class="person-dialog">
                                                                            <div class="person-dialog__image img-fit rounded">
                                            <img width="450" height="600" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAcIAAAJYAQMAAADLw3S+AAAABlBMVEUAAAD///+l2Z/dAAAAAXRSTlMAQObYZgAAAAlwSFlzAAAOxAAADsQBlSsOGwAAADhJREFUeNrtwQENAAAAwqD3T20PBxQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAD8G4fwAAHAiGHlAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC" class="attachment-3:4@450 size-3:4@450 lazyload" alt=""  decoding="async"  data-src="https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-450x600.jpeg" data-srcset="https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-450x600.jpeg 450w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-960x1280.jpeg 960w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-150x200.jpeg 150w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-300x400.jpeg 300w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-850x1133.jpeg 850w" data-sizes="auto" data-eio-rwidth="450" data-eio-rheight="600" /><noscript><img width="450" height="600" src="https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-450x600.jpeg" class="attachment-3:4@450 size-3:4@450" alt="" sizes="(max-width: 340px) 90vw, 300px" decoding="async" srcset="https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-450x600.jpeg 450w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-960x1280.jpeg 960w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-150x200.jpeg 150w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-300x400.jpeg 300w, https://www.arcolatheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Robin-hooper-Headshot-850x1133.jpeg 850w" data-eio="l" /></noscript>
                                        </div>
                                    
                                    <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                        <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                            <h2 class="type-h3">Robin Hooper</h2>

                                                                                            <p class="type-h5">Knut Brovik</p>
                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Theatre includes: Seasons with the Liverpool Everyman, Glasgow Citizens and Half Moon Theatres. </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">John Paul George Ringo and Bert</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Lyric Shaftesbury Avenue), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bloody Poetry, Star Gazy Pie </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Royal Court Theatre), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bright Room Called Day </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Bush) </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Public </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Theatre Royal Stratford East), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Art of Success</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> ( Paines Plough), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pamela</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Shared Experience), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Country Wife, Lady Windermere’s Fan</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Cambridge Theatre Company), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Saturday Sunday Monday </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Chichester), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Importance of Being Earnest</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Nottingham), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">What the Butler Saw </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Northampton), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dead Funny</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (York and Bolton), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">My Night With Reg </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Stoke on Trent)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Television includes: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Walter, Martin Chuzzlewit, The Office, Monarch of the Glen, Riot at the Rite, Twenty Twelve, Mrs Biggs, Lucan, Quacks, The Nevers and January Nights.</span></i></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Plays written for the theatre include: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Move </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(NT Platform and Tour), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Astonish Me</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Not the RSC Festival), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Queer Fish </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(BAC), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Free from Sorrow</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Tristan Bates), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not the Love I Cry For </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Arcola), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Love Your Soldiers </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">(Sheffield Crucible Studio), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Foul Pages</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (The Hope Theatre) and </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Broken Lad</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Arcola Outside / Published Aurora Metro Books). Previously Literary Manager for both Paines Plough New Writing Theatre Company and The Royal Court Theatre.</span></p>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </article>
                            </template>
                                            </li>
                                                                                                                                        
