                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Deniz Dortok is a London-based sound designer, composer and performer working across theatre, film, opera and contemporary classical music. He recently completed his Master’s degree in Composition at the Royal College of Music (RCM) with Distinction. His work includes </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Toffee</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (BFI London, Straight 8 winner), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Catfish the Cabaret</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Edinburgh Fringe), and </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Sequel</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (King’s Head Theatre), where his music was praised for enhancing the narrative’s mystical and eerie qualities. Other recent works include </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Nocturna</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, a concept album released on Berlin label re:natura exploring light pollution, a chamber piece for Riot Ensemble, and a short opera composed in collaboration with Tête à Tête and the RCM Vocal &amp; Opera Department.</span></p>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </article>
                            </template>
