                        <div class="person__header">
                            <h3 class="type-h6">Rob Kelly</h3>

                                                            <p class="type-body-s">Casting Director</p>
                            
                            <div class="person__header__flex">
                                
                                                            </div>
                        </div>

                                                    <template data-dialog-content="dialog-person-6-7963">
                                <article class="person-dialog">
                                    
                                    <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                        <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                            <h2 class="type-h3">Rob Kelly</h2>

                                                                                            <p class="type-h5">Casting Director</p>
                                                                                    </div>

                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio margin-trim type-body-l">
                                            <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Rob Kelly is an Emmy nominated London based Casting Director working across theatre, film and television. Known for championing exceptional new talent alongside established performers.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Television includes: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Geek Girl</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Netflix), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Curfew</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Paramount+), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Phoenix Rise</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (BBC Three), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Quiet Hour</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Wild</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Village Idiot</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Intruder</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Never Too Late</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Channel 5), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Free Rein</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Netflix), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Gangsta Granny Strikes Again</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (BBC), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Drowning</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Netflix), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pandora</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (The CW), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whitstable Pearl</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (AMC), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dodger</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (BBC), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Hard Cell</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Netflix)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Film Includes: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ace</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Netflix), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Fing!</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Sky), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">How to Date Billy Walsh</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Amazon MGM Studios), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Robin and the Hoods</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Sky), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Something in the Water</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (StudioCanal), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">This Is Christmas</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Sky)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Theatre includes: </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Hadestown</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (West End &amp; UK Tour), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Who Killed Marilyn</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (West End), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Allegra</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (West End), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Private Jones</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Southwark Playhouse), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Jonathan Larson Project</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Southwark Playhouse), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Little Shop of Horrors</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Liverpool Playhouse &amp; Hope Mill Theatre), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Driving Miss Daisy</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (York Theatre Royal), </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Most Favoured</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">This Bitter Earth</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (Soho Theatre)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">www.robkellycasting.com</span></p>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </article>
                            </template>
                                            </li>
                            </ul>
